{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Private Methods\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 fakeApiRequest()\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 private suspend fun fakeApiRequest()\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Purpose:} Demonstrates coroutine timeout handling and sequential execution with timeout.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Features:} - Uses {\f1 withTimeoutOrNull(1900)} for timeout handling - Executes two sequential API calls - Updates UI with results or timeout message - Switches context between IO and Main threads\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Execution Flow:} 1. Calls {\f1 result()} and updates UI 2. Calls {\f1 result2()} and updates UI 3. If operations exceed 1900ms, displays timeout message\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Example:}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 // Internal usage within onClick listener\line
CoroutineScope(Dispatchers.IO).launch \{\line
    fakeApiRequest()\line
\}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 fakeApiRequest1()\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 private suspend fun fakeApiRequest1()\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Purpose:} Demonstrates concurrent coroutine execution using {\f1 async} and {\f1 awaitAll}.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Features:} - Concurrent execution of multiple suspend functions - Uses {\f1 async} for parallel processing - Waits for all operations to complete with {\f1 awaitAll}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Execution Flow:} 1. Creates two async coroutines for {\f1 result()} and {\f1 result2()} 2. Waits for both to complete 3. Updates UI with combined results\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Example:}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 // Alternative implementation (currently commented out)\line
private suspend fun fakeApiRequest1() \{\line
    withContext(Dispatchers.IO) \{\line
        val result = async \{ result() \}\line
        val result2 = async \{ result2() \}\line
        val deferred = awaitAll(result, result2)\line
        setResult(deferred)\line
    \}\line
\}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 setResult(result: String)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 private suspend fun setResult(result: String)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Purpose:} Updates the UI with a single result string.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Parameters:} - {\f1 result: String} - The text to append to the current display\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Behavior:} - Switches to Main dispatcher for UI updates - Appends new result to existing text with newline separator - Thread-safe UI updates\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Context Switching:}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 withContext(Dispatchers.Main) \{\line
    val newText = tvResult.text.toString() + "\\n$result"\line
    tvResult.text = newText\line
\}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 setResult(deferred: List)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 private suspend fun setResult(deferred: List<String>)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Purpose:} Updates the UI with multiple results from concurrent operations.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Parameters:} - {\f1 deferred: List<String>} - List of results from concurrent coroutines\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Behavior:} - Switches to Main dispatcher for UI updates - Combines all results into a single display string - Thread-safe UI updates\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Usage:}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 withContext(Dispatchers.Main) \{\line
    val newText = "$\{deferred[0]\} $\{deferred[1]\}"\line
    tvResult.text = newText\line
\}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 result()\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 private suspend fun result(): String\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Purpose:} Simulates a long-running API call or background operation.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Returns:} {\f1 String} - Always returns \u8220"Result\u8221"\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Behavior:} - Introduces 5-second delay using {\f1 delay(5000)} - Simulates network or database operation - Non-blocking suspension\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Example:}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 val apiResult = result() // Takes 5 seconds to complete\line
println(apiResult) // Prints: "Result"\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 result2()\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 private suspend fun result2(): String\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Purpose:} Simulates another long-running API call or background operation.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Returns:} {\f1 String} - Always returns \u8220"Result2\u8221"\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Behavior:} - Introduces 5-second delay using {\f1 delay(5000)} - Simulates network or database operation - Non-blocking suspension\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Example:}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 val apiResult = result2() // Takes 5 seconds to complete\line
println(apiResult) // Prints: "Result2"\par}
